---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="How I work" description="Decisions first, licence-clean by design, evidence over claims, zero-trust defaults, and AI-assisted delivery under human governance.">
  <article class="stack-lg">
    <header class="stack">
      <p class="eyebrow">Practice</p>
      <h1>How I work</h1>
      <p class="lede">The habits that make architecture hold up after the slide deck.</p>
    </header>

    <ul class="rule-list prose">
      <li><span class="n">01</span><div><strong>Decisions first.</strong> Every significant choice is an ADR that names the options, the trade-offs and the consequences.</div></li>
      <li><span class="n">02</span><div><strong>Licence-clean by design.</strong> Permissive licences only, checked in CI, with any exception recorded and justified.</div></li>
      <li><span class="n">03</span><div><strong>Evidence over claims.</strong> Static checks and live results are reported separately. Every live result is a dated receipt, and nothing is "done" until a tester signs it off.</div></li>
      <li><span class="n">04</span><div><strong>Zero-trust defaults.</strong> Default-deny networking, verified identity on every hop, least privilege everywhere.</div></li>
      <li><span class="n">05</span><div>
        <strong>AI-assisted delivery, human-governed.</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>An AI architect writes the architecture and work orders and reviews every change.</li>
          <li>An AI implementer codes one work order at a time.</li>
          <li>I own the product, set the quality targets and sign off.</li>
          <li>No agent approves its own work.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></li>
      <li><span class="n">06</span><div><strong>Frameworks I practise:</strong> TOGAF ADM, C4, DDD, ISO/IEC 25010 quality characteristics, and PCI DSS 4.0.</div></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
